  {
   "MatterHistoryAccelaRecordId": null,
   "MatterHistoryActionBodyId": 138,
   "MatterHistoryActionBodyName": "Metropolitan Council",
   "MatterHistoryActionDate": "2026-07-21T00:00:00",
   "MatterHistoryActionId": 391,
   "MatterHistoryActionName": "passed on second reading",
   "MatterHistoryActionText": "The bill was approved by the Planning Commission, the Budget and Finance Committee and the Planning and Zoning Committee. Council Member Horton moved that the bill be passed on second reading, which motion was properly seconded. Council Member Benedict called for the previous question, which motion was seconded and failed by the following roll call vote: Yes (20): Suara, Porterfield, Toombs, Gamble, Cortese, Capp, Benedict, Harrell, Eslick, Evans, Bradford, Huffman, Horton, Druffel, Gadd, Nash, Benton, Sepulveda, Lee, and Spain; No (15): Evans-Segall, Hill, Kimbrough, Parker, Welsch, Vo, Cash, Kupin, Taylor, Preptit, Johnston, Ellis, Rutherford, Styles, and Ewing; Abstain (1): Allen. Council Member Horton amended the previous motion and moved that the bill be passed on second reading with a re-referral to the Budget and Finance Committee, which motion was properly seconded. After discussion, Council Member Spain called for the previous question, which motion was seconded and approved by the following roll call vote: Yes (32): Suara, Porterfield, Evans-Segall, Hill, Toombs, Gamble, Cortese, Parker, Capp, Benedict, Harrell, Evans, Bradford, Huffman, Vo, Cash, Kupin, Horton, Taylor, Druffel, Gadd, Preptit, Johnston, Nash, Benton, Ellis, Sepulveda, Rutherford, Styles, Lee, Ewing, and Spain; No (3): Kimbrough, Eslick, and Welsch; Abstain (1): Allen. The matter recurred on the motion that the bill be passed on second reading with a re-referral to the Budget and Finance Committee, which motion was seconded and approved by the following roll call vote: ",
